## Request

Add the smallest complete shared authority compatibility contract. Define one normalized resolver
for absent database, file authority, shadow import, qualified shadow, Hybrid authority, and recovery.
Route all consumers that currently infer authority from database presence or schema support through
that contract, including readiness, planning order, Doctor, dashboard/reporting, PRM, campaign, and
index behavior.

Make file-authoritative fallback fully coherent before adding the broader convergence orchestrator.
Reproduce GitHub issue #66 with a released-style 0.52.1 empty schema-2 shadow and a file-backed
`ready-for-prm` Idea Brief; assert that every relevant consumer sees the same authority, identity,
artifact count, and bounded feature limits. Include a populated unqualified shadow fixture so
compatibility never silently trusts imported database content.

Stop after focused implementation proof, strict Doctor, configured development-lane verification,
the exact Work2 candidate registration, and a durable Hybrid checkpoint. Do not force conversion or
cutover, publish, tag, release, synchronize clients, close issue #66, begin M2, or mutate the
`workpc` firmware workspace in this campaign.

