## Result

The shared resolver now keeps retained files authoritative for absent, file, unqualified shadow,
and checkpoint-qualified shadow states; selects SQLite only after explicit Hybrid cutover; and
fails corrupt or contradictory authority closed with a bounded recovery action. Readiness,
planning order, document dispatch, Doctor, campaign/PRM guidance, index behavior, and dashboard
inventory use that decision. File-backed reporter identities are stable UUIDs, lifecycle values
and timestamps satisfy the hosted contract, and unavailable Hybrid outcome features remain
explicit.

The released-style 0.52.1 regression covers empty and populated schema-2 shadows; a database-only
decoy cannot displace the retained Idea, roadmap, or campaign. The same snapshot then proves
qualified-shadow remains file-authoritative until guarded cutover and exercises corrupt-database
recovery.

